BT /F2 16 Tf 56 762.8 Td (SMS-07 Bunkering Procedure) Tj ET
BT /F2 13 Tf 56 720.7 Td (Safety Management System Procedure: Fuel Oil Bunkering Operations) Tj ET
BT /F2 13 Tf 56 678.7 Td (Purpose) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 56 649.7 Td (The objective of this procedure is to establish a standardized, safe, and environmentally) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 56 635.2 Td (compliant protocol for the transfer of fuel oil \(bunkering\) aboard the vessel. This document) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 56 620.7 Td (ensures that all personnel involved in bunkering operations understand their roles, adhere) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 56 606.2 Td (to strict safety limits, and maintain effective communication with the bunker barge crew.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 56 591.7 Td (The primary goals are to prevent pollution incidents, ensure the structural integrity of) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 56 577.2 Td (storage tanks, and protect the health and safety of the crew during high-risk transfer) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 56 562.7 Td (operations. Compliance with this procedure is mandatory for all personnel involved in the) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 56 548.2 Td (bunkering process.) Tj ET
BT /F2 13 Tf 56 506.1 Td (Responsibilities) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 56 477.1 Td (The operational hierarchy for bunkering is clearly defined to ensure accountability and) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 56 462.6 Td (command clarity. The Chief Engineer holds the ultimate authority and is the person in charge) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 56 448.1 Td (of bunkering. As the responsible officer, the Chief Engineer must oversee the entire) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 56 433.6 Td (operation from preparation through to completion. This includes verifying tank availability,) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 56 419.1 Td (authorizing the start of transfers, and making critical decisions regarding weather) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 56 404.6 Td (conditions or equipment failures.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 56 375.6 Td (The Bunker Barge Master and their crew are responsible for providing fuel that meets the) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 56 361.1 Td (agreed specifications and for maintaining safe pumping operations on the barge side. They) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 56 346.6 Td (must coordinate closely with the vessel's engineering team to synchronize flow rates and) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 56 332.1 Td (pressures. All other crew members assigned to the bunkering station, including duty) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 56 317.6 Td (engineers and deck ratings, are responsible for executing physical tasks such as plugging) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 56 303.1 Td (scuppers, monitoring gauges, and responding to alarms under the direct supervision of the) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 56 288.6 Td (Chief Engineer.) Tj ET
BT /F2 13 Tf 56 246.6 Td (Pre-bunkering Meeting) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 56 217.6 Td (Effective communication is the cornerstone of safe bunkering. A pre-bunkering safety meeting) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 56 203.1 Td (with the barge crew must be held before any physical connection or transfer begins. This) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 56 188.6 Td (meeting serves as a formal interface between the vessel and the supplier to align on) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 56 174.1 Td (operational parameters, emergency contacts, and stop-work criteria. During this session, the) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 56 159.6 Td (Chief Engineer will review the bunker delivery note, confirm tank capacities, and discuss) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 56 145.1 Td (the specific sequence of operations.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 56 116.1 Td (Crucially, the checklist must be signed by both parties during this meeting. This signature) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 56 101.6 Td (confirms that both the vessel and the barge have reviewed the safety requirements, verified) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 56 87.1 Td (equipment readiness, and agreed to the operational limits. No transfer shall commence until) Tj ET
BT /F1 8 Tf 56 28 Td (SMS-07 Bunkering Procedure \(fictional\) - page 1 of 3) Tj ET
endstream
