BT /F1 10 Tf 56 771.5 Td (this document is fully executed and filed in the engine room logbook. The meeting should) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 56 757.0 Td (also cover communication methods, such as radio channels or hand signals, to be used if) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 56 742.5 Td (voice contact is lost during the operation.) Tj ET
BT /F2 13 Tf 56 700.4 Td (Checklist) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 56 671.4 Td (Prior to initiating any physical work, the team must conduct a thorough pre-transfer) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 56 656.9 Td (inspection using the approved Bunkering Checklist. This systematic verification ensures that) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 56 642.4 Td (all safety barriers are in place and that the vessel is prepared to receive fuel without) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 56 627.9 Td (risk of overflow or pollution. The checklist items must be physically verified and ticked) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 56 613.4 Td (off by the responsible crew members before proceeding.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 56 584.4 Td (Key preparatory actions include verifying that scuppers must be plugged and the SOPEP locker) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 56 569.9 Td (opened before starting. Plugging scuppers prevents any potential spill from entering the) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 56 555.4 Td (sea, while opening the SOPEP \(Shipboard Oil Pollution Emergency Plan\) locker ensures that) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 56 540.9 Td (immediate access to absorbent materials, booms, and disposal bags is available at the bunker) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 56 526.4 Td (station. Additionally, the team must verify that all overfill alarms are functional, tank) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 56 511.9 Td (gauges are calibrated, and emergency stop buttons are clearly visible and unobstructed.) Tj ET
BT /F2 13 Tf 56 469.9 Td (During Transfer) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 56 440.9 Td (The actual transfer of fuel oil requires constant vigilance and strict adherence to pumping) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 56 426.4 Td (parameters. The operation begins with a cautious approach to identify any leaks or blockages) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 56 411.9 Td (early. Transfer starts at a reduced rate for the first 10 minutes. This initial low-flow) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 56 397.4 Td (period allows the crew to inspect all connections, flanges, and hoses for signs of leakage) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 56 382.9 Td (before increasing the volume. If no issues are detected after this period, the flow rate may) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 56 368.4 Td (be increased to normal operating levels, subject to pressure constraints.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 56 339.4 Td (Pressure management is critical to prevent hose bursts or flange failures. The maximum) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 56 324.9 Td (pumping pressure 5 bar unless agreed otherwise. This limit must be strictly monitored by the) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 56 310.4 Td (duty engineer on the vessel and confirmed with the barge operator. Any deviation from this) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 56 295.9 Td (pressure limit requires immediate investigation and potential cessation of pumping.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 56 281.4 Td (Throughout the transfer, the Chief Engineer or their designated representative must) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 56 266.9 Td (continuously monitor tank levels to prevent overfilling. Tanks must not be filled above 90%) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 56 252.4 Td (of capacity. This margin is essential to accommodate thermal expansion of the fuel and wave-) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 56 237.9 Td (induced vessel motion, which could otherwise cause an overflow.) Tj ET
BT /F2 13 Tf 56 195.8 Td (Completion) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 56 166.8 Td (Upon reaching the target volume or when the transfer is complete, the Chief Engineer must) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 56 152.3 Td (authorize the shutdown of pumps on both the vessel and the barge. The lines must be drained) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 56 137.8 Td (and disconnected according to standard isolation procedures. All valves must be closed and) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 56 123.3 Td (locked out where necessary to prevent accidental ingress of fuel or seawater. The bunker) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 56 108.8 Td (delivery note must be signed by both parties, confirming the quantity received and noting) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 56 94.3 Td (any discrepancies in quality or quantity.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8 Tf 56 28 Td (SMS-07 Bunkering Procedure \(fictional\) - page 2 of 3) Tj ET
